---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import fish from "../../data/fish.json";

const top = [...fish]
  .filter((f) => Number(f.meat_per_day) > 0)
  .sort((a, b) => Number(b.meat_per_day || 0) - Number(a.meat_per_day || 0))
  .slice(0, 12);
---

<Base
  title="Best Fish to Farm in Dave the Diver - DiverDB"
  description="Best Dave the Diver fish for the ranch based on meat per day, breeding rate and farm capacity."
>
  <h1>Best Fish to Farm for the Ranch</h1>
  <p class="muted">
    Ranch value is not about the biggest fish. It is about stable daily meat output.
  </p>

  <h2>What makes a good farm fish</h2>
  <p>
    The Marinca ranch rewards species with high <strong>meat per day</strong>, a reasonable
    <strong>breeding rate</strong> and enough <strong>breed cap</strong> to keep production running.
    Rare fish with enormous size are usually worse farm animals because they occupy capacity for
    lower daily yield.
  </p>

  <h2>Top farm candidates from the data</h2>
  <div style="overflow-x:auto">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Fish</th>
          <th>Zone</th>
          <th>Meat / day</th>
          <th>Farm meat avg</th>
          <th>Breed cap</th>
          <th>Breed rate</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {top.map((f) => {
          const zone = (f.categories || []).find((c) => c !== "Fish" && c !== "Bosses") || f.source || "Unknown";
          return (
            <tr>
              <td><strong>{f.title}</strong></td>
              <td>{zone}</td>
              <td>{f.meat_per_day}</td>
              <td>{f.farm_meat_avg}</td>
              <td>{f.breed_cap}</td>
              <td>{f.breed_rate}</td>
            </tr>
          );
        })}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Ranch strategy</h2>
  <p>
    Start with one or two species that match your current restaurant ingredients. Keep the farm
    lean until you unlock more tank capacity, then add the best producers from the table above.
    Use the <a href="/tools/fish-farm/">Fish Farm Planner</a> to filter by zone and minimum meat
    per day as you unlock new regions.
  </p>
</Base>
